# agibridge — canonical F-1 hobby framing banned-word regex
# Single source of truth (C4) sourced by:
#   - backend pre-commit hook (brief-backend-dev.md DoD #3)
#   - DevOps CI workflow (brief-devops-automator.md DoD #1)
#   - Tech Writer README+landing CI grep (brief-technical-writer.md DoD #3)
#
# Applied to:
#   - app/static/**            (every file: HTML/JS/CSS/MD)
#   - openapi.json             (post-generation, piped through jq)
#   - route decorator strings  (extracted from app/api/**/*.py via ast.parse)
#   - README.md / agibridge/landing/**
#   - HF Space README.md `short_description` field
#
# EXEMPT (legitimate technical references, NOT user-facing):
#   - app/api/**/*.py Python comments and log strings
#   - test fixtures
#   - CHANGELOG.md (allowlist for upstream issue references)
#
# Format: one Python regex per line. CI tooling reads this file, OR-joins, applies with re.MULTILINE.
# Word boundaries (\b) are explicit. Phrases preserve internal whitespace via \s+.

# --- Original W1 list (from spec §10 v1) ---
\bproduct\b
\bservice\b
\bcompany\b
\bcustomers\b
\bclients\b
\bpricing\b
\btier\b
\bpaid\b
\bsubscription\b
\bpremium\b
free\s+trial
sign\s+up
sign\s+in
log\s+in
\blogin\b
\blogout\b
\baccount\b
your\s+data
we\s+collect
we\s+store

# --- Added per CR-5 (RC v1 review of W1 spec) ---
\bsubscribers\b
\btrial\b
\bplan\b
\bbuy\b
\bpurchase\b
\bcheckout\b
\binvoice\b
\bpayment\b
we\s+offer
our\s+solution

# --- End of canonical list (v1, 2026-05-02). ---
# Updates require:
#   1. Discussion in DECISION REQUEST format (this is F-1 positioning, not boilerplate)
#   2. Bump revision date in spec v2.2 §10
#   3. Update this file + bump comment header date
